# Chaos: the helper's rotation against our server (Lua only; applies after 0001-0051).
# - Every cast of the magic shooter (spells and runes) and of the healing waits for the server's answer before the
#   spell goes out again: overlay module game_helperrotation (ChaosHelperRotation). The server's cooldown packets
#   (onSpellCooldown / onSpellGroupCooldown, g_game signals) confirm a cast; no answer within 1.2 s (3 round trips on a
#   slow line) means refused and that spell backs off 2-16 s while the rest of the rotation goes on. The shooter held
#   a spell the server refused (level, target, a missing corpse or chi) on a 200 ms loop for ever and the spells below it
#   in its group never went out; with a round trip over 200 ms the next spell of a group went into the group cooldown.
#   The helper's own 200 ms pre-cooldowns no longer pass for server packets.
# - The shooter's casts go through the 0026 rate guard (helperCastAllowed) too.
# - The shooter checks the level (and skips spells the server does not have, notOnServer); healing checks class, level
#   and mana, so a heal the server refuses no longer ends the priority loop before the heal below it.
# - A spell entry's vocations are the server's ids (game_chaosspells): a class casts a spell when its own id is listed.
# - A self-centred Chaos attack spell (no area table) needs a monster within 3 sqm instead of always counting one.
# - A spell that needs a target is targetable even with an area (Radiant Shard).
# - While a cast-time spell charges (ChaosHelperRotation.CAST_MS, or game_castbar says so) the shooter casts nothing
#   and a heal waits unless health is below 50%: any other spell interrupted it and the server refunded its cooldown.
# - Magic shield: the server has no spell that ends it; the "exana" option does nothing instead of shouting the words
#   (or Bushido Focus, which took id 245) and no longer holds the shooter's support spells back.
--- a/mods/game_helper/helper.lua
